</tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t1-fn1"><label/><p>Abbreviations: BHD&#x0003d;Birt&#x02013;Hogg&#x02013;Dub&#x000e9;; ND&#x0003d;Not determined owing to the unavailability of matched normal tissue.</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn2"><label>a</label><p>For <italic>BHD,</italic> c. corresponds to coding sequence relative to ATG in exon 4 (Genbank accession number <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="NM&#x0005f;144997" ext-link-type="gen"/>). Numbers in brackets are refering to the previous nomenclature used (Genbank accession number <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="AF517523" ext-link-type="gen"/>).</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn3"><label>b</label><p>For <italic>TP53</italic>, c. corresponds to coding sequence according to ATG in exon 2 (Genbank accession number <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="NM&#x0005f;000546" ext-link-type="gen"/>).</p></fn><fn id="t1-fn4"><label>c</label><p>Not a silent mutation because it involves the last base of exon 4 and has been reported to be responsible for exon skipping.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Polymorphisms detected in <italic>BHD,</italic> <italic>TP53</italic>, and <italic>HNF1&#x003b2;</italic> genes in 92 sporadic renal tumours</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="5" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff